{"format":2,"id":"classical","name":"Name That Tune: Classical","icon":"🎻","color":"#7C5CBF","category":"music","subcategory":"classical","version":1,"description":"Hear a famous classical theme and name the piece. The sooner you know it, the harder you hit.","question":"Name this piece!","typeable":false,"skillNoun":"Overture","cards":[{"id":"fur-elise","prompt":"♪","answer":"Für Elise","alts":["Fur Elise","Bagatelle No. 25"],"options":["Moonlight Sonata","Ode to Joy","Rondo alla Turca"],"fact":"Beethoven wrote it around 1810, but it was only published in 1867, forty years after his death.","difficulty":1,"audio":{"melody":"E5:.25 D#5:.25 | E5:.25 D#5:.25 E5:.25 B4:.25 D5:.25 C5:.25 | A4:.5 R:.25 C4:.25 E4:.25 A4:.25 | B4:.5 R:.25 E4:.25 G#4:.25 B4:.25 | C5:.5 R:.25 E4:.25 E5:.25 D#5:.25 | E5:.25 D#5:.25 E5:.25 B4:.25 D5:.25 C5:.25 | A4:.5 R:.25 C4:.25 E4:.25 A4:.25 | B4:.5 R:.25 E4:.25 C5:.25 B4:.25 | A4:1.5 || R:2 | A2:.25 E3:.25 A3:.25 R:.75 | E2:.25 E3:.25 G#3:.25 R:.75 | A2:.25 E3:.25 A3:.25 R:.75 | R:1.5 | A2:.25 E3:.25 A3:.25 R:.75 | E2:.25 E3:.25 G#3:.25 R:.75 | A2:1.5","tempo":72,"voice":"piano"}},{"id":"ode-to-joy","prompt":"♪","answer":"Ode to Joy","alts":["Beethoven's Ninth","Symphony No. 9 finale"],"fact":"The choral finale of Beethoven’s Ninth Symphony (1824), written when he was almost completely deaf; it is now the anthem of the European Union.","difficulty":1,"audio":{"melody":"F#4:1 F#4:1 G4:1 A4:1 | A4:1 G4:1 F#4:1 E4:1 | D4:1 D4:1 E4:1 F#4:1 | F#4:1.5 E4:.5 E4:2 | F#4:1 F#4:1 G4:1 A4:1 | A4:1 G4:1 F#4:1 E4:1 | D4:1 D4:1 E4:1 F#4:1 | E4:1.5 D4:.5 D4:2 || D3:4 | A2:2 D3:2 | D3:2 A2:2 | D3:2 A2:2 | D3:4 | A2:2 D3:2 | D3:2 A2:2 | A2:2 D3:2","tempo":150,"voice":"strings"}},{"id":"beethoven-5","prompt":"♪","answer":"Beethoven's Symphony No. 5","alts":["Beethoven's Fifth","Fifth Symphony","Symphony No. 5"],"options":["Mozart's Symphony No. 40","Toccata and Fugue in D minor","In the Hall of the Mountain King"],"fact":"Beethoven’s Fifth (1808) opens with